From: Vividh Yadav <178728541+VividhDesign@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:07:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Add SQ8 scalar quantization with exact re-ranking and
 memory-mapped vectors

- quantization="sq8": the graph stores one byte per dimension (per-dimension
  min/max), searched with asymmetric AVX2/NEON kernels.
- rerank=True (default) keeps the float32 vectors outside the graph blocks,
  builds the graph at full precision and re-ranks the ef candidates exactly.
  rerank=False drops them for an index about 3x smaller.
- Index.load(path, mmap_vectors=True) memory-maps the re-rank vectors, so only
  the graph and codes stay resident.
- Ranges widen while the index has fewer than 1,000 vectors, so one-by-one
  upserts do not freeze a degenerate range.
- Index format v2 (v1 files still load). Exposed in Python, Collection and
  the REST server; benchmark script gains strata-sq8 / faiss-sq8 and GloVe-6B.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
